course: dictionary
lesson: 5302
title: Learning a word from a sentence
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A dictionary tells you what a word means, but the sentence around it often gives more clues. «A newborn kangaroo is about the size of a jelly bean; it crawls into its mother's pouch.» The sentence tells you the pouch is somewhere a tiny baby can crawl into and stay, so it must be a kind of pocket on the mother.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Kangaroo usually names an animal, but in «kangaroo court» it is part of a phrase. A kangaroo court is an unfair, unofficial trial. The word court shows you that the phrase is about a trial, not an animal.
explain: Check your guess by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. If the sentence still makes sense, your clue has worked. If it does not, read on, look for more clues, or check a dictionary.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Kangaroo» means a large Australian animal that hops on strong back legs and has a long, thick tail.
fact: A baby kangaroo is called a joey, and it lives in its mother's pouch.
fact: «Kangaroo court» means an unfair, unofficial trial.
fact: Marsupials are mammals with pouches, such as kangaroos and koalas.
exercise: Which animal hops on strong back legs and carries its baby in a pouch? | A snake | A horse | *A kangaroo | A rabbit
exercise: Leo says a kangaroo court is a court full of kangaroos. What does kangaroo court mean? | *An unfair, unofficial trial | A trial held outdoors in the bush | A fair and official trial | A court with kangaroos as judges
exercise: «A newborn kangaroo crawls into its mother's pouch.» Find and copy the word that names the place the baby crawls into. | *pouch | mother's | newborn | crawls
test: «Marsupials, such as kangaroos and koalas, carry their tiny newborns in a pouch.» What is a marsupial? | A bird that lays eggs | A fish that lives in the sea | A tree that grows in the desert | *An animal with a pouch for its babies
test: Ella reads, «The trial was a kangaroo court: the verdict was decided before anyone spoke.» What does kangaroo court suggest? | A trial held in a zoo | A fair trial with a judge and jury | *A trial that was unfair and not official | A fun game for children
exam: «The red kangaroo is the largest marsupial and can hop at over fifty kilometres an hour.» What does largest mean? | Fastest of its kind | *Biggest of its kind | Smallest of its kind | Oldest of its kind
